it's been a safe assumption that  developer monolith have been working on  a follow-up to their 2014 Game of the  Year middle-earth  shadow of Mordor while it seems retailer  target may have leaked the game details  and release date of the still  unannounced game as spotted by neogaf  user death by backlog a listing for  middle-earth shadow of war appeared on  targets international website the since  removed listing featured box art along  with a short description and a release  date of August 22nd it reads go behind  enemy lines to forge your army conquer  fortresses and dominate Mordor from  within experience how the award-winning  Nemesis system creates unique personal  stories with every enemy and follower  and confront the full power of the Dark  Lord Sauron and his ring rates in this  epic new story of middle-earth details  on a gold edition of the game are also  listed in addition to the base game it  will apparently include two Nemesis  expansions slaughter tribe and outlaw  tribe featuring new enemies followers  missions abilities weapons fortress and  wilderness updates and a mythic gear set  it will also feature two new story  expansions called the blade of Galadriel  and the desolation of Mordor the Gold  Edition listing also gives a little more  detail on the game itself teasing the  ability to forge a new ring of power  conquer fortresses in massive battles  and dominate Mordor with your personal  or army this isn't the first mention of  a sequel to shadow of Mordor  early last year stunt performer lauren  mary kim's online resume mentioned she  worked on shadow of Mordor - for  everything middle-earth and all the  details on shadow of war as they arrived  hit subscribe if you're on YouTube and  keep it locked to GameSpot
 

